{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540198-some-guidance-with-picking-my-character-s-spirit-heritage","id":1540198,"title":"Some Guidance with picking my Character's Spirit-Heritage...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-12T03:39:08-07:00","id":1540198,"title":"Some Guidance with picking my Character's Spirit-Heritage...","content":"First things first, my character is a Lupus Theurge belonging to the Fianna Tribe. Who's Kin-Fetch found him after his first change at a Whiskey Distillery when he drank several barrels of the stuff completely and passed out. He might have died from alcohol poisoning was he not a Garou, let alone one belonging to Lady Fianna. Being a Wild Wolf, he adopted the name 'Keg' As in Keg of Ale, however his deed name is 'One-with-the-Spirits', which could be construed as having more than one meaning if you get it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, during the character creation process I splashed out giving all five of his Background points to Spirit-Heritage... Question is, what type of spirit and how should it manifest with him. I know it's my choice, but I need some guidance here. Looking for something suitable...<br /> <br /> Please advise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","user":"Wolf-Man","date":". 08-12-2024, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T07:44:52-07:00","id":1540203,"title":"","content":"If I may ask, how did the wolf end up drinking whiskey in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T08:52:36-07:00","id":1540208,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm seconding this question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T14:34:26-07:00","id":1540222,"title":"","content":"I was hoping this wouldn't happen, and even my storyteller hasn't bothered with this yet. I'm really still working that one out and had this idea that a couple of barrels fell off the back of a truck (unknown to the truck driver...) somewhere near where the road meets the wilderness that my Wolf occupies and started leaking from the fall. Well, my wolf might have come along and started licking up the contents (The Whiskey...) Of course, this is far from what I originally said. In my original idea, my wolf prematurely access's his werewolf or Garou powers to break into the distillery or maybe some spirits (Not Whiskey Spirits, but some Umbral-Entities...) do that for him. Maybe there was a bane or some wyrmey things at the distillery that needed investigation and he was lead there by benevolent spirits where he invertedly noticed a few barrels that had been broken and felt the famous thirst of the Fianna come over him. Does this explain things to you or do uyou want better. all I can really say is that this is just a game, and that it's horror too if you think Wolves drinking whiskey sounds irresponsible.<br /> <br /> Perhaps if you can do better, maybe help me out with that too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T14:36:05-07:00","id":1540223,"title":"","content":"BTW, your question is a little off topic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","user":"Wolf-Man","date":". 08-12-2024, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:05:28-07:00","id":1540224,"title":"","content":"A Nexus-Crawler attacks a pack of Garou at a Whiskey Distillery. As the place gets wrecked, my wolf wanders in out of curiosity and maybe something more, being potential Garou himself. However, his thirst overtakes him when he notices some broken barrels and jumps inside one to drink it all. He's eventually found passed out by the pack of Garou who by that time have gotten rid of the Nexus-Crawler and they find out he's Garou too.<br /> <br /> He survived, because he Wolfed out into his Crinos or Hispo shape to help battle the effects of Whiskey poisoning and was later given the gift of Resist Toxin as a brand new Fianna pup.<br /> <br /> Sorry, for letting a poor wolf get drunk and dangerously close to dying from the effects of poisoning, (I would never let this happen in real life though...) but this is the World of Darkness...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","user":"Wolf-Man","date":". 08-12-2024, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:20:13-07:00","id":1540228,"title":"","content":"Alcohol isn't pleasant to wolves, and is far more toxic than for us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:31:31-07:00","id":1540230,"title":"","content":"I feel like &quot;magical drunk Irish&quot; is an incredibly xenophobic stereotype to be playing to. I suggest maybe reading up a little on historic brehon law to find culturally grounded character inspiration that doesn't have to play to extremely negative calvinist stereotypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T16:13:50-07:00","id":1540234,"title":"","content":"As bad as it sounds, this is the World of Darkness here and your replies are not helping me one bit. I just wanna play a Irish wolf that enjoys his grog. Surely there can be room for that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T16:25:17-07:00","id":1540235,"title":"","content":"Leaving aside the whole whiskey thing which seems irrelevant to the Heritage question anyway I would suggest <b>Airitech</b> as the spirit heritage. Draw the mechanics from Old Wolf of the Woods and have a hatred for Kinfolk who consort with the Sidhe to betray the Garou and your good to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T16:33:29-07:00","id":1540236,"title":"","content":"I definitely didn't mean to offend anyone. I'm from Australia where there is a big culture of drinking. So, I guess I didn't realize the offense I had caused. I do appreciate the pointer to the historical Brehon laws. I'll do some more research to fill out other facets of my character...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T16:36:01-07:00","id":1540237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540198-some-guidance-with-picking-my-character-s-spirit-heritage?p=1540235#post1540235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving aside the whole whiskey thing which seems irrelevant to the Heritage question anyway I would suggest <b>Airitech</b> as the spirit heritage. Draw the mechanics from Old Wolf of the Woods and have a hatred for Kinfolk who consort with the Sidhe to betray the Garou and your good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for actually answering my question. This will help me alot...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T16:42:25-07:00","id":1540238,"title":"","content":"I think it's fun to have a lupus have their First Change and instead of accidentally killing people, just found a barrel of alcohol and got drunk until he passed out. If I was the ST, I'd certainly allow it. Alcohol isn't poisonous to the Garou, and I might have even allowed your character to start already having the Gift Resist Toxin as a result of your experience.<br /> <br /> Since Spirit Heritage is basically Pure Breed for a particular type of spirit, it's really a question of what mix of flavor text and in-game benefits you want and that your ST will approve. Here are some options I think may make sense for your character.<br /> <br /> One possibility is to go with something like Stag's Brood so that any spirits allied with Stag treat you well. That does happen to include the Grain spirit, which is the spirit of grain alcohol. Although your ST will probably want access to the Axis Mundi sourcebook, or at the very least figure out what kind of specific spirits fall under Stag.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is to go with Plant Spirits. That again might possibly cover Grain (depending if you interpret grain alcohol as a plant spirit, or its own kind - but at the very least you would cover various grains before they were turned into alcohol), and other plant spirits like Oak that happens to be allied to Stag. Since many plant spirits are wary of Garou because of their Rage, your character's greater ease at dealing with them would set him apart. Again, access to the Axis Mundi sourcebook would probably help your ST here.<br /> <br /> You might also want a narrower slice of animal spirits, maybe prey animals in general, cervidae, woodland mammals, or something similar. Find whatever mix works best for you. That would fit a general theme of Stag even if it excludes large parts of its brood and includes lots of other animals that normally are not under Stag.<br /> <br /> Another option would be something like the spirits of alcohol, or the spirits of beverages (alcoholic and non-alcoholic) in general. There are various talens that are based on beverages, and there are folklore about when people blackout from alcohol, it is because the spirit of the alcohol is possessing them. This would require a lot of additional work for yourself and your ST to figure out the individual spirits and their abilities, but it would set you up nicely to be a Fianna brewer and making various beverage talens. You would probably want access to both Fianna tribebooks for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T16:48:19-07:00","id":1540239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf-Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540198-some-guidance-with-picking-my-character-s-spirit-heritage?p=1540236#post1540236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely didn't mean to offend anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>We now live in a society where not only are people easily offended for things, they try wielding their being offended as a weapon against others.<br /> <br /> &quot;My character likes to drink&quot; is a perfectly fine trait for any character in many games. Is it a bit stereotypical for the Fianna? Yes, but so what? There is a drinking culture in the Fianna, as well as other tribes I would add. There's still a lot of distance between &quot;My character likes to drink&quot; and &quot;Obnoxious drunk Irish&quot; stereotype. The only people who can really judge is yourself and your own gaming group. You don't need to justify your gaming choices to anyone here.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T16:57:04-07:00","id":1540240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540198-some-guidance-with-picking-my-character-s-spirit-heritage?p=1540238#post1540238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fun to have a lupus have their First Change and instead of accidentally killing people, just found a barrel of alcohol and got drunk until he passed out. If I was the ST, I'd certainly allow it. Alcohol isn't poisonous to the Garou, and I might have even allowed your character to start already having the Gift Resist Toxin as a result of your experience.<br /> <br /> Since Spirit Heritage is basically Pure Breed for a particular type of spirit, it's really a question of what mix of flavor text and in-game benefits you want and that your ST will approve. Here are some options I think may make sense for your character.<br /> <br /> One possibility is to go with something like Stag's Brood so that any spirits allied with Stag treat you well. That does happen to include the Grain spirit, which is the spirit of grain alcohol. Although your ST will probably want access to the Axis Mundi sourcebook, or at the very least figure out what kind of specific spirits fall under Stag.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is to go with Plant Spirits. That again might possibly cover Grain (depending if you interpret grain alcohol as a plant spirit, or its own kind - but at the very least you would cover various grains before they were turned into alcohol), and other plant spirits like Oak that happens to be allied to Stag. Since many plant spirits are wary of Garou because of their Rage, your character's greater ease at dealing with them would set him apart. Again, access to the Axis Mundi sourcebook would probably help your ST here.<br /> <br /> You might also want a narrower slice of animal spirits, maybe prey animals in general, cervidae, woodland mammals, or something similar. Find whatever mix works best for you. That would fit a general theme of Stag even if it excludes large parts of its brood and includes lots of other animals that normally are not under Stag.<br /> <br /> Another option would be something like the spirits of alcohol, or the spirits of beverages (alcoholic and non-alcoholic) in general. There are various talens that are based on beverages, and there are folklore about when people blackout from alcohol, it is because the spirit of the alcohol is possessing them. This would require a lot of additional work for yourself and your ST to figure out the individual spirits and their abilities, but it would set you up nicely to be a Fianna brewer and making various beverage talens. You would probably want access to both Fianna tribebooks for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome reply","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T17:02:23-07:00","id":1540241,"title":"","content":"It could be that the smell of whiskey triggered the First Change, and then he went for the barrels already in Crinos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T16:07:59-07:00","id":1540307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540198-some-guidance-with-picking-my-character-s-spirit-heritage?p=1540238#post1540238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fun to have a lupus have their First Change and instead of accidentally killing people, just found a barrel of alcohol and got drunk until he passed out. If I was the ST, I'd certainly allow it. Alcohol isn't poisonous to the Garou, and I might have even allowed your character to start already having the Gift Resist Toxin as a result of your experience.<br /> <br /> Since Spirit Heritage is basically Pure Breed for a particular type of spirit, it's really a question of what mix of flavor text and in-game benefits you want and that your ST will approve. Here are some options I think may make sense for your character.<br /> <br /> One possibility is to go with something like Stag's Brood so that any spirits allied with Stag treat you well. That does happen to include the Grain spirit, which is the spirit of grain alcohol. Although your ST will probably want access to the Axis Mundi sourcebook, or at the very least figure out what kind of specific spirits fall under Stag.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is to go with Plant Spirits. That again might possibly cover Grain (depending if you interpret grain alcohol as a plant spirit, or its own kind - but at the very least you would cover various grains before they were turned into alcohol), and other plant spirits like Oak that happens to be allied to Stag. Since many plant spirits are wary of Garou because of their Rage, your character's greater ease at dealing with them would set him apart. Again, access to the Axis Mundi sourcebook would probably help your ST here.<br /> <br /> You might also want a narrower slice of animal spirits, maybe prey animals in general, cervidae, woodland mammals, or something similar. Find whatever mix works best for you. That would fit a general theme of Stag even if it excludes large parts of its brood and includes lots of other animals that normally are not under Stag.<br /> <br /> Another option would be something like the spirits of alcohol, or the spirits of beverages (alcoholic and non-alcoholic) in general. There are various talens that are based on beverages, and there are folklore about when people blackout from alcohol, it is because the spirit of the alcohol is possessing them. This would require a lot of additional work for yourself and your ST to figure out the individual spirits and their abilities, but it would set you up nicely to be a Fianna brewer and making various beverage talens. You would probably want access to both Fianna tribebooks for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that answer. I guess I was looking in the wrong books. Our groups uses the 20th Anniversary Edition books for our game. Not sure if we are limited to them as well. I have every edition with most of the books and recall the Axis Mundi. It's pity that the 20th Editions didn't have their own version of that one or even the tribal volumes. <br /> <br /> As for Spirit Heritage being like the Pure Breed background for a Particular Spirit. I also picked Pure Breed as well eventually putting 5 points into that as well as Ancestors (Creating alot more work for myelf and my ST). Now if there are Spirits of Alcohol or Beverages, that may work out sufficiently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T18:41:31-07:00","id":1540320,"title":"","content":"There are spirits of quite literally everything, including alcohol beverages. Though I would suggest you consider other spirit heritages that are less one note than &quot;alcohol,&quot; because right now they read like a one-off gag--deed name is alcohol related, First Change is alcohol related, spirit heritage is alcohol related (and an alcohol pun), the tribe is alcohol related...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T20:13:02-07:00","id":1540326,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bp-k91zsMtI&amp;t=30s\" target=\"_blank\">The Bard's Tale: Remastered and Resnarkled - The Beer Song! (youtube.com)</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T04:24:09-07:00","id":1540340,"title":"","content":"That dead horse moving any faster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T10:42:05-07:00","id":1540368,"title":"","content":"The spirits of <i>uskebeaghe</i> would I think be spirits of man. The grain is domesticated, the fermenting yeast is domesticated, and the water is clarified and purified by human processes. The story of Whiskey is a profoundly human story, as is the story of Resist Toxin as humans have a tolerance for, and even enjoyment of, poison that most other creatures of the natural world lack. For cursory reading it seems as though the history of whiskey distilling in Ireland has its origin in medicinal and alchemical purposes. The terroir of whiskey is said to be a distillation of the land from which it hails, especially true with Scotch which may be fermented using heat from peat soil. <br /> <br /> With the history and nature of distilled spirits and the fact that it was a catalyst to your lupus wolf awakening to their shifter nature, I'd be inclined to give you a spirit heritage to man/human spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T10:46:22-07:00","id":1540369,"title":"","content":"Thanks, what book it this from or is this from the Axis-Mundi - Book of Spirits...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T20:44:10-07:00","id":1540411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540198-some-guidance-with-picking-my-character-s-spirit-heritage?p=1540368#post1540368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirits of <i>uskebeaghe</i> would I think be spirits of man. The grain is domesticated, the fermenting yeast is domesticated, and the water is clarified and purified by human processes. The story of Whiskey is a profoundly human story, as is the story of Resist Toxin as humans have a tolerance for, and even enjoyment of, poison that most other creatures of the natural world lack. For cursory reading it seems as though the history of whiskey distilling in Ireland has its origin in medicinal and alchemical purposes. The terroir of whiskey is said to be a distillation of the land from which it hails, especially true with Scotch which may be fermented using heat from peat soil.<br /> <br /> With the history and nature of distilled spirits and the fact that it was a catalyst to your lupus wolf awakening to their shifter nature, I'd be inclined to give you a spirit heritage to man/human spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>That word, I have found to be the old English and Gaelic word for Whiskey. <a href=\"https://www.bing.com/search?q=uskebeaghe+-+origin+and+definition&amp;qs=n&amp;form=QBRE&amp;sp=-1&amp;ghc=1&amp;lq=0&amp;pq=uskebeaghe+-+origin+and+definition&amp;sc=0-34&amp;sk=&amp;cvid=EBAC48FCB09842E799CC27EFF5924A60&amp;ghsh=0&amp;ghacc=0&amp;ghpl=\" target=\"_blank\">uskebeaghe - origin and definition - Search (bing.com)</a> Is it used in any of the Werewolf books at all, and if so which one?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T20:45:45-07:00","id":1540412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540198-some-guidance-with-picking-my-character-s-spirit-heritage?p=1540235#post1540235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving aside the whole whiskey thing which seems irrelevant to the Heritage question anyway I would suggest <b>Airitech</b> as the spirit heritage. Draw the mechanics from Old Wolf of the Woods and have a hatred for Kinfolk who consort with the Sidhe to betray the Garou and your good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>This looks interesting as well. I trust it's used in the books. I don't think I have found it yet... I'm so terrible at research...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T09:22:45-07:00","id":1540435,"title":"","content":"Sorry yes, I could've been clearer. When I used to do tabletop wargames there was a faux pas called the chip test wherein you tried to see if your own miniature's painting (or worse someone else's) could withstand being chipped with a fingernail and still look authentic. I tend to like to run my ttRPGs in a way that players can look under that first layer of paint and the world, characters and motives still make sense. An easy way of doing that is a little bit of wikipedia - encyclopedia and etymonline -etymology dictionary to give me a sense of what the real life story is before I start tweaking things to be what I need for my games. U<i>skebeaghe</i> was the indigenous Irish word for whiskey.<br /> <br /> Airitech is not a term I'm familiar with but seems to be the name of some people/creatures with wolf shapeshifting in the legendary era of Fiann McCool (the real-ish person that the fictional Fianna Garou are named after.)<br /> <br /> Spirits of Man don't seem to exist in a lot of WtA books, I kindof just assumed they did; but almost the gifts I had associated with them seem to be from Ancestor spirits anyways, so I'd just adjudicate them as being a subset of that brood.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:30:01-07:00","id":1540459,"title":"","content":"The game doesn't really provide any kind of comprehensive spirit broods or other groups of spirits. The most we get is found in Axis Mundi and only covers the most obvious groups (the tribal spirit totems and other big groups - plants, minerals, ancestors, etc.) The game just doesn't have any kind of comprehensive groupings or even spirits. So we're never given examples of other kind of spirit broods, not even for the totems of the lost tribes or other Changing Breeds. Or for powerful Incarna that don't have Fera or tribes, but probably have their own broods. Or any division of groups within greater groups - why should &quot;plants&quot; all be one category when we don't have &quot;animals&quot;? We could easily do that, but in practice most people would probably want to divide them up. Especially when it comes to something like Spirit Heritage. The default categories can work fine for a lot of STs and players, but others will want something less generic.<br /> <br /> So it is really up to the ST to consider other kinds of groupings and the kinds of spirits found there. This is both an opportunity (lots of customization if the ST wants) and a burden (it puts a lot of work on the ST).<br /> <br /> That's one reason I created a thread trying to figure out other possible Spirit Broods, the best Incarna to head them, and what kinds of spirits would fall under them. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1410223-additional-spirit-broods\">That thread is located here</a>.<br /> <br /> But spirit heritage isn't necessarily limited to actual broods. They could conceivably be any kind of grouping (even informal ones). It's just about what makes sense to the player and is approved by their ST.<br /> <br /> For example, if you find alcohol too limiting, maybe you want something like spirits of Fermentation. That would include anything that creates alcohol, but also other kinds of fermentations - beans, dairy products, condiments, bread and other grains, pickled fruits and vegetables, meats, beverages, bokashi, industrial chemicals, etc. This kind of group probably would not be that useful in a Werewolf game and you wouldn't want to spend Background points for it, but it could make an interesting NPC (or even PC) who really wants to work on brewing, cooking, or even chemistry. Of course, the ST would need to create such spirits from scratch and work with the PC on what kind of benefits that might bring. And why a lupus (or indeed any Garou) would have a Spirit Heritage of this sort would be hard to explain.<br /> <br /> So it's probably best to think of less specific and more general groups that make sense for the Fianna overall. Figure out a few general ideas that seem most interesting/beneficial to you and discuss with your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T16:55:53-07:00","id":1540479,"title":"","content":"Humans don't have any spiritual reflections in W:tA. Mage says that they don't in the Spirit Wilds but do in the Astral Umbra, which Garou basically never go to and whose spirits they don't interact with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T12:50:39-07:00","id":1540525,"title":"","content":"Humans usually do not have any spiritual reflections in the Penumbra. However, any humans in the Periphery do present some reflection, and &quot;spiritually advanced&quot; people do have reflections. Sleeping people who have chimares are supposed to be present as well. So while the Penumbra is mostly empty of people and do not reflect the masses of humanity actually present in the Realm, it is up to the ST to determine if it is completely empty or if there are reflections present and their number and frequency.<br /> <br /> I think many STs will default to be completely empty because running any scene in the Umbra tends to take more effort and decision making by the ST than anything set in the physical world. Why give yourself another thing to consider? But those who do want an opportunity to introduce certain NPCs or situations by having human reflections appear in the Penumbra are justified in doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T21:40:56-07:00","id":1540607,"title":"","content":"I have chosen Farm-to-Table as Keg's Spirit Heritage. Where it can be found in the W20 book &quot;Umbra - The Velvet Shadow&quot; on page 137. You would no doubt let me know if this bothers you or/and seems wrong or inappropriate to you. Otherwise, thanks for all your assistance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T02:11:32-07:00","id":1540612,"title":"","content":"Going just a bit off subject and still concerning the very same character...<br /> <br /> Is it ever possible for my character's Ancestor Spirit to be of a different tribe to the one he belongs to. I was thinking of the very first Werewolf/Garou character I ever played. Which was actually given to me as a handout to play as at a gaming convention in North Brisbane back in the mid 90's. (I understand back then it was 2nd Edition with a different name for that background...) but the adventure we were in that day (A one-shot, of course...) is called Thermidor was something to do with that Revolution in France (Storm the Bastille!) long ago and my character, an Bone Gnawer, born under the no-moon and born to four legs named in his human shape as one Jaques Henriot. He was with the peasants in this and fought well. I also played him well, winning a trophy (shown :slight_smile: ) for best portrayal of said character. Anyway, can you see where this is going? Well, if I can dig up that old character sheet. Maybe they could be my character's ancestor spirit. I may have to retcon that he was really Irish wolf/Garou that found itself in France due to the transient nature of some Bone Gnawers being homeless and having access to Umbral Portals. I may have to add rank to his character sheet as well. Seeing as Ancester Spirits are most commonly heroes themselves. If this is possible, it would be kind of cool, but my real problem now is actually finding that character sheet...<img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" borde